    "note": "ClientHello, HTTP/2 frames and header sets are those captured for safari-18.0-macos; wreq-util declares safari 18.3.1 to use the same TLS and HTTP/2 configuration (safari18_3_1: tls_options!('2', 'CIPHER_LIST_2', 'SIGALGS_LIST_2'), http2_options!(3)). The User-Agent is wreq-util's; accept-language is wreq-util's. Nothing was seen on the wire for this version here. wreq-util declares these to differ from 18.0 by dropping ecdsa_sha1 from the signature algorithms; the captured 18.0 already sends the list without it, so the hello is 18.0's."
